{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe .bridge_state/projects.json write path is a HAND-ROLLED client that bypasses the\nauthoritative shared store seams and thereby violates the tickets-branch invariant\n(every mutation runs under the unified write lock AND auto-commits+publishes).\nprojects_store._write_record hand-rolls tempfile+os.replace instead of the shared\nfsutil.atomic_write, and projects_store.set_project/remove_project never take the lock,\ncommit, or push. This forced the ad-hoc hand-commits behind incident\n05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27 (LEG/ONE/TWO/ZERO leak).\n\n## Scope: CONVERT the hand-rolled client to the authoritative shared seams ONLY\nReuse the existing seams exactly as-is. Do NOT modify any seam and do NOT build a facade\nover them (that would be additional, separately-approved scope):\n- rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write — the shared crash-atomic file write.\n- rebar._store.lock.write_lock — the unified tickets write lock (context manager).\n- rebar._store.push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, *, message=...) — commits all\n  pending tracker changes UNDER THE WRITE LOCK (+ rebase guard) then pushes.\n\n## Approach (pure conversion)\n1. projects_store._write_record: replace the hand-rolled mkstemp/fdopen/os.replace block\n   with `fsutil.atomic_write(path, json.dumps(record, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")`.\n   Behavior-preserving: the on-disk bytes stay byte-identical, and the existing\n   `path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` is KEPT before the call (atomic_write\n   requires the parent dir to already exist), so first-write still creates .bridge_state.\n   The module's read path stays stdlib-only standalone; the write path lazily imports the\n   rebar._store seams (only ever reached from the _lib_ops library layer, never from the\n   engine reconciler's read-only importers), and the module docstring is updated to state\n   this read-path-standalone / write-path-uses-seams split so the swap does not contradict\n   the documented invariant.\n2. Run the mutation under the lock AND publish it, both through existing seams, from the\n   single _lib_ops entry point that BOTH the CLI and the library route through\n   (bridge_projects_set / bridge_projects_remove -> set_project / remove_project): hold\n   `lock.write_lock(tracker)` around the read-modify-write call to set_project/remove_project\n   (so the RMW itself runs under the lock — no lost-update race), release it, then call\n   `push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, message=\"bridge: update projects mapping\")`\n   (which re-acquires the same lock for the commit+push). No ad-hoc git; the read path\n   (load_mapping / read_projects) is untouched.\n3. Record the invariant (explicitly requested): add the two-part invariant to\n   docs/concurrency.md \"Mutating the tracker\" section — EVERY tickets-branch mutation runs\n   under write_lock AND auto-commits+publishes.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope (separate tickets)\n- Write-time project-key VALIDATION — separate ticket 209b (a distinct behavior addition,\n  not a seam conversion).\n- Any change to resolve_project / legacy_default (ticket a011).\n- Any modification of the shared seam or a new facade/helper over it (needs separate\n  approval).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] projects_store._write_record uses `fsutil.atomic_write` (not hand-rolled\n      mkstemp/os.replace) and keeps the `path.parent.mkdir(...)`; serialized bytes are\n      byte-identical to today, pinned by a RED-first test in\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_happy.py`.\n- [ ] A projects.json mutation runs its read-modify-write under `lock.write_lock` and is\n      then committed + pushed via `push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, ...)` with no\n      ad-hoc git; verified by a seam-patched regression guard in\n      `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_projects_happy.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` \"Mutating the tracker\" section states the two-part invariant:\n      EVERY tickets-branch mutation runs under write_lock AND auto-commits+publishes.\n- [ ] No new commit/push/lock/atomic-write helper or facade is introduced; the existing\n      seams are used as-is (checked: `git diff` shows only inline seam call-sites added).\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_happy.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_projects_happy.py -q`\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`\n\n## Sequencing\nEdits projects_store.py + docs/concurrency.md (+ tests); reuses push/fsutil/lock (no edit).\nDisjoint from A/C/D. Ticket 209b (key validation) and ticket E (parity conversion) both\nedit projects_store.py / the reconciler commit path and are sequenced AFTER this one.","title":"Bridge-state writes: adopt shared write_lock + commit+push + atomic_write seams (tickets-branch invariant)"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786809438645759001,"uuid":"ee0a456a-3775-468d-9242-39561852a085"}